---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Deployments and promotion — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-querial-sky">For DevOps</p>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-1">Deployments and promotion</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <p>
                Design is not deployment. Bind a published version to an EnvironmentKind,
                map logical connections (already on the steps) to this project's endpoints,
                set parameter values, optionally attach a schedule and agent-pool bindings.
                Parameters are per deployment — do not bake production secrets into step SQL.
            </p>

            <h2>Promotion</h2>
            <p>
                Promotion clones the exact pipeline version, package hash, and Git commit
                if present. It never modifies SQL content. Source deployment parameters
                clone to the target; secrets stay ciphertext, not decrypted in the wizard.
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Development and Staging: DevOps may promote. Auto-approval when the kind does not require approval.</li>
                <li>Production: RequiresApproval. DevOps sees development + staging in the wizard; Production is hidden unless CanAdminProject. Even if the HTTP attribute were wrong, PromotionService fails closed for DevOps on Production promote and approve.</li>
                <li>Pending promotions are approved or rejected by Project admin (including Team-admin inherit and Platform admin). Rejection archives the target deployment and records the actor snapshot.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Bindings</h2>
            <p>
                Per-step deployment bindings carry agent pool and assignment mode
                (automatic, specific agent, pool, tag expression, round robin). They do
                not remap connections. Pool assignment is snapshotted when the run plan
                is created.
            </p>

            <h2>Multi-tenant pattern</h2>
            <p>
                The same version can run for hundreds of tenant databases. Each
                deployment has independent run history. A failure on tenant A does not
                mutate the version used by tenant B.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
